Contract-call log records now omit full function_args and return_value fields at the default info level. Set STACKS_LOG_CLARITY_VALUES=1 to restore these fields in the existing records without enabling global debug logging. Debug and trace include the fields by default; STACKS_LOG_CLARITY_VALUES=0 suppresses them at every level. The setting is read once per process and applies to text and JSON logs.
Contract-publish payload and transaction dumps containing full source are now omitted from problematic-transaction and proposal-rejection logs at the default info level. Set STACKS_LOG_CONTRACT_SOURCE=1 to restore them independently of contract-call values, or =0 to suppress them even with debug/trace enabled.
When a payload dump is suppressed, it is replaced by contract_name (address.contract-name) and, for calls, function_name. Suppressed proposal-rejection tx dumps are replaced by txid. Setting the corresponding variable to 1 restores the original full-detail field set instead of these replacements.
Contract-call payload dumps in problematic-transaction and proposal-rejection logs now follow STACKS_LOG_CLARITY_VALUES. Full analysis-error expressions follow STACKS_LOG_CONTRACT_SOURCE; bounded diagnostics and source locations remain at info.
Unexpected P2P response info logs now report the message type and peer instead of dumping message contents.
Problematic-transaction logs now encode origin using the transaction network instead of always using testnet addresses. Mainnet log consumers must match the corrected mainnet address in both summary and full-detail records; the detail flags do not restore the incorrect encoding.
